# --- Required -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A ZeroID service key (zid_sk_...) for the tenant/project you are evaluating.
# Generate it in Studio -> Settings -> API Keys, or take the agent-gateway key shown on an
# adopted agent in Studio -> Registry. With no key set, every script skips (exit 2) rather
# than failing, so nothing runs against a real tenant by accident.
HIGHFLAME_API_KEY=

# --- Endpoints (defaults target Highflame SaaS / prod) --------------------------------
# Point these at any environment you are running the PoV against. For a dev cluster the
# hosts are typically auth-dev.highflame.dev / api-dev.highflame.dev / gateway-dev.highflame.dev.
# HIGHFLAME_AUTHN_URL=https://auth.highflame.ai
# HIGHFLAME_SHIELD_URL=https://api.highflame.ai
# HIGHFLAME_GATEWAY_URL=https://gateway.highflame.ai

# --- Optional --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HIGHFLAME_HTTP_TIMEOUT=30

# For the custom-identifier recipe (03-dlp), the internal ID format to prove detection on.
# The default matches an "EXL-####" study/case id. Change the regex to your real format.
# EXELIXIS_CASE_ID_REGEX=\bEXL-\d{4}\b

# --- SCIM provisioning proof (02-authorization/scim_provisioning.py) -------------------
# The UC8 trigger demo drives admin's inbound SCIM 2.0 provider as if it were Okta/Entra.
# It needs the SCIM base URL and a per-tenant SCIM bearer token (hfscim_...), minted by an
# org admin: POST $ADMIN_URL/v1/admin/scim/tokens {"name": "pov-demo"} — the plaintext is
# shown exactly once. With either unset the script skips (exit 2).
# Dev cluster base: https://control-dev.highflame.dev/scim/v2 (prod: control.highflame.ai).
# HIGHFLAME_SCIM_URL=
# HIGHFLAME_SCIM_TOKEN=
